1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,531
Haloalkanes are classified by the carbon that carries the halogen.

2
00:00:04,531 --> 00:00:08,502
If that carbon is joined to one other carbon, it is primary.

3
00:00:08,502 --> 00:00:10,403
Two others, secondary.

4
00:00:10,403 --> 00:00:11,940
Three, tertiary.

5
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,802
This is not just bookkeeping.

6
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:21,705
It decides the mechanism: primary halides react by S N two, tertiary ones by S N one.

